cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to this talk, please cite it as below."
title: "Setting the legal limit with an R package: from lone scripter to open-source regulatory infrastructure"
abstract: >-
  Conference talk on fifteen years of building open-source R software for
  environmental management and regulation — from an unreproducible 2012
  expert-elicitation tool, through R packages and GitHub collaboration
  (FSSgam, epower, bayesnec, ssdtools), to the adoption of ssdtools as the
  default software for deriving water quality guideline values in Australia,
  New Zealand and Canada — and on what changed, and what did not, with the
  arrival of AI coding assistants.
type: software
authors:
